            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="KIN07" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Lord</roleName>
                        <forename>George</forename>
                        <surname>Kinnaird</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1805-10-11"/>
                    <occupation>seventh Lord Kinnaird of Inchture</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Entered under 1795 in the 1796 lists, and duly appears on 17 March 1795
    at William Bosville's. Kinnaird one of the sixteen Scottish representative peers. The dinner at Bosville's
   seems to be his only appearance. A mention of Kinnaird in 1807, an adv at a Joseph Johnson
    dinner, is after the seventh Lord's death and likely to refer to the eighth Lord, Charles Kinnaird, 
    politician and art collector, who is in the <title>DNB</title>.  The final mention of the name, in 1828, is after the eighth Lord's death so might be the
    ninth Lord.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
